>> title: Salsa Verde Cruda
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: tomatillo, chiles, mexican, vegetarian, no-cook
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: salsa cruda, raw salsa verde, salsa verde crudo, green table salsa, salsa de molcajete, uncooked salsa verde
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, carnitas
>> servings: 6
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: rinse the stickiness off, quarter
>> step.2: blend in short pulses
>> step.3: stir in, rest 10 min

Rinse @tomatillos{3/4%lb}(340 g; husked) under warm running water until the sticky film is gone, then quarter them.

Blend @&(~1)tomatillos{} with @serrano chiles{2}(stemmed), @garlic{1%clove}, @white onion{2%Tbs}(chopped), and @kosher salt{1%tsp} in short pulses, stopping while it is still loose and pale green rather than smooth.

Stir @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped), @white onion{1/4%cup}(finely chopped), and @fresh lime juice{2%tsp} into @&(~1)salsa{}, and let it ~rest{10%min} for the raw chile to come forward.
